<title>GERMANY: Rexrodt says point of no return on EMU crossed.</title>
<headline>Rexrodt says point of no return on EMU crossed.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Economics Minister Guenter Rexrodt said on Monday that Europe had crossed the point of no return in its goal of establishing a single currency for members of the 15-nation bloc.  </p>
<p>Rexrodt said there was no alternative to launching European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) in 1999 as planned.</p>
<p>&quot;The point of no return has been crossed,&quot; Rexrodt told a forum on EMU in Koenigswinter near Bonn.</p>
<p>He said European Union members hoping to join the single currency must stick to the timetable and strict fiscal criteria.</p>
<p>The Maastricht treaty calls for strict limits on public debt and budget deficit ratios by 1998 in order for member states to be eligible for a single currency in 1999.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
